Two things must be done on a machine with network access before release:

  1. Replace <COPYRIGHT HOLDER> above with the name the copyright belongs to.
     PolyForm names this party the "licensor", and it is who reserves the
     commercial rights — so it must be a real legal name, not a handle.

  2. Replace everything below the line at the bottom of this file with the
     complete, verbatim text of the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0, from:

         https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0/

The text was deliberately NOT reproduced from memory when this file was created.
A license is a legal document and has to be byte-exact; the machine this repo
was renamed on had no network access, and a subtly wrong license is worse than
an obviously missing one.

What this license does, in short (not a substitute for the real text):

  - The source may be read, forked, modified and shared.
  - Use is limited to noncommercial purposes. Personal use and use by
    noncommercial organizations qualify; selling it, or using it to make money,
    does not.
  - The commercial rights stay with the licensor, so nobody else may sell this
    or a derivative of it.

Bundled third-party components (FFmpeg, ONNX Runtime and the Rust dependency
tree) keep their own separate licenses, which are NOT affected by this file.
See packaging/common/THIRD-PARTY.md.

Detector model weights are downloaded at runtime, are not part of this
repository, and carry their own licenses — each one is recorded in the model
registry (crates/ob-core/src/registry.rs) and shown by `obscura models list`.

